  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday Night through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1130 AM CDT Wed May 27 2026\n\nThe sluggish Omega block pattern will stay with us going into the\nweekend. We will keep the humid conditions as a couple of waves \nwith deep moisture gradually pivot across the area. This will \nincrease rain coverage again area-wide for late Friday into \nSaturday. High PW values suggest potential for some more local \nheavy downpours for at least the first half of the weekend. \n\nScattered shower chances linger into Sunday, but we will begin to\nfeel the beginning of a pattern change as the trough over the \neast coast deepens and forces dry north flow into TN. Dry \nconditions will take hold as we go into the next work week. We \nwill enjoy some deep blue skies again. Temperatures will be near \nnormal levels, except slightly cooler than normal at night. \nHumidity will drop off to comfortable levels. Heading into late \nnext week, we will have gradually increasing temperatures as we \nmove into a more typical early summer pattern.",
